			<description><![CDATA[
<p>Cybercriminals are harnessing AI not to break in, but to make sense of their stolen loot and increase their leverage in multi-million dollar ransomware heists. This episode unpacks how AI is now turbocharging extortion and negotiations on the dark side.</p><ul> 
<li>The "bone crushing" didn't happen this month.</li> 
<li>Revisiting and inspecting July's Patch Tuesday.</li> 
<li>A widespread and worrisome flaw in OpenSSL.</li> 
<li>Claude can now access your 1Password credentials.</li> 
<li>Bitwarden is aware that we need whole new security.</li> 
<li>The day ends in "y" so a new prompt injection attack.</li> 
